                %li
                  %a{:href => "#exotica_leptoquarks_bosons_etc"}
                    Exotica: Leptoquarks,
                    = succeed "-bosons," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Z
                            %mo ′
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z'
          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general_idea General idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            asserts that the fundamental quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} physical fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            are modeled as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            to a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            – called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            – is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"}> special
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+groups"} unitary groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = SU(3) \times SU(2) \times U(1)
            (or rather a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of this by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z/6
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "standard+model+of+particle+physics#GaugeGroup"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            used to form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            looks fairly ad hoc on first sight.
          %p
            A
            %strong grand unified theory
            (“GUT” for short) in this context is an attempt to realize the standard model as sitting inside a conceptually simpler
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+particle+physics%29"} model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            is a bigger but
            %em simpler
            group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{G}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
            in the technical sense, which contains
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenologically
            viable if a process of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
            at some high
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            scale – the “GUT scale” – would reduce the model back to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            without adding spurious extra effects that would not be in agreement with existing observations in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
          %p
            The terminology “grand unified” here refers to the fact that such a single simple group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{G}
            would unify the fundamental
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forces"} forces
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+nuclear+force"} weak nuclear force
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
            in a way that generalizes the way in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electroweak+field"} electroweak field
            already unifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+nuclear+force"} weak nuclear force
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
          %p
            Since no GUT model has been fully validated yet (but see for instance
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#FongMeloni14"} Fong-Meloni 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
            “beyond the
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            and hence unify not just the three gauge forces but also the fourth known fundamental force, which is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            plus the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+everything"} theory of everything
          %p
            (Here it is important to remember the context, both “grand unified” and “of everything” refers to aspects of presently available models of fundamental physics, and not to deeper philosophical questions of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ontology"} ontology
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length+scales"} length scales
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            (from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmic
            scales, over
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            around the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electroweak+symmetry+breaking"} electroweak symmetry breaking
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT+scale"} GUT scale
            and
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+scale"} Planck scale
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ScalesInFundamentalPhysics.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "flavour+in+particle+physics#Zupan19"} Zupan 19
          %h3#IdeaofSU5GUT
            The
            = succeed "-GUT" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
          %p
            The argument for the hypothesis of “grand unification” is fairly compelling if one asks for
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+objects"} simple algebraic structures
            in the technical sense (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+groups"} simple Lie groups
            and their
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
          %p
            The
            %em exact
            gauge group of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            is really a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi SM
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_{SM}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big( U(1) \times SU(2) \times SU(3) \big) / \mathbb{Z}_6
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_6
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} acts freely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{
                  \\simeq \big( U(1) \times SU(2) \times SU(3) \big) / \mathbb{Z}_6  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  S \big( U(2) \times U(3)\big)
                  }}
                  \\;\subset\;
                  SU(5)
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(5)
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09, p. 33-36
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
          %p
            Moreover, the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi SM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{SM}
            that captures one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generation+of+fundamental+particles"} generation of fundamental particles
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi SM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{SM}
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09, table 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            it is simply
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi SM
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Λ
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V_{SM} \simeq \Lambda \mathbb{C}^5
          %p
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09, p. 36-41
          %p
            This leads to the
            = succeed "-GUT" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            %a{:href => "#GeorgiGlashow74"} Georgi-Glashow 74
          %h3#dseries_guts D-Series GUTs
          %h4#TheGUTKnownAsSO10
            The
            = succeed "-GUT" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10)
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10)
          %p
            There is a further inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5) \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%2810%29"} Spin(10)
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            in 10 (Euclidean) dimensions (still a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generation+of+fundamental+particles"} generation of fundamental particles
            regarded as an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda \mathbb{C}^5
            as
            %a{:href => "#IdeaofSU5GUT"} above
            extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09, theorem 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generation+of+fermions"} generation
            rep
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi SM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{SM}
            is now identified as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi SM
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 16
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V_{SM} \;\simeq\; \mathbf{16} \oplus \overline{\mathbf{16}}
