          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToProtonDecay Relation to proton decay
          %p
            Many GUT models imply that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton"} proton
            – which in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            is a stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
            (of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KM14"} KM 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} Experimental
            searches for such
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton+decay"} proton decay
            (see there for more) put strong bounds on this effect and hence heavily constrain or rule out many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
          %p
            But in recent years it is claimed that there are in fact realistic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
            that do not imply any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton+decay"} proton decay
            = succeed "-models" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#MuetterRatzVaudrvange16"} Mütter-Ratz-Vaudrvange 16
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FornalGrinstein17"} Fornal-Grinstein 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FornalGrinstein18"} Fornal-Grinstein 18
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-Higgs+grand+unification"} gauge-Higgs grand unification
            such as
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%2811%29"} Spin(11)
            = succeed "\u201D-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%2811%29"} SO(11)
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%2812%29"} Spin(12)
            = succeed "\u201D-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%2812%29"} SO(12)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HosotaniYamatsu15"} Hosotani-Yamatsu 15
            %a{:href => "#FuruiHosotaniYamatsu16"} Furui-Hosotani-Yamatsu 16, Sec. 2.6
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hosotani17"} Hosotani 17, Section 6
          %h3#RelationToNeutrinoMasses Relation to neutrino masses
          %p
            The high energy scale required by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/seesaw+mechanism"} seesaw mechanism
            to produce the experimentally observer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
            masses happens to be about the conventional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT+scale"} GUT scale
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Mohapatra06"} Mohapatra 06
          %blockquote
            %p
              I also noted at the same time that interactions between a pair of lepton doublets and a pair of scalar doublets can generate a neutrino mass, which is suppressed only by a factor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{-1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              could produce observable neutrino oscillations. The subsequent confirmation of neutrino oscillations lends support to the view of the Standard Model as an effective field theory, with M somewhere in the neighborhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 10
                        %mn 16
                      %mi GeV
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10^{16} GeV
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "neutrino#Weinberg09"} Weinberg 09, p. 15
          %p
            Detailed matching of parameters of non-supersymmetric
            = succeed "-GUT" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            is discussed in
            %a{:href => "#OhlssonPernow19"} Ohlsson-Pernow 19
          %h3#RelationToLeptoquarks Relation to leptoquarks
          %p
